notolog (1.2.2-1ubuntu1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Update Notolog Editor to version 1.2.2.
  * Keep packaged settings isolated on the first launch of a fresh profile.
  * Build runtime-dispatched llama.cpp CPU backends on amd64 while retaining a
    portable arm64 build.
  * Validate the binary marker, application version, and target architecture.
  * Re-audit and smoke-test the executable after Debian package processing.
  * Verify licence coverage for distributions embedded in the executable.
  * Include psutil attribution and correct dual-licence expressions.
  * Restrict package metadata to the supported amd64 and arm64 architectures.
  * Update the Python build frontend to version 1.6.0.
  * Enforce the minimum supported Ubuntu glibc baseline in release builds.

 -- Vadim Bakhrenkov <dev@notolog.app>  Sun, 30 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

notolog (1.2.1-1ubuntu1) resolute; urgency=medium

  * Update Notolog Editor to version 1.2.1.
  * Include llama.cpp support in the standalone package.
  * Harden asynchronous shutdown and encrypted-file handling.
  * Improve status bar file information and responsive icons.
  * Update the PyInstaller and Python build toolchain.
  * Refresh pinned GitHub Actions and build-validation hooks.
  * Correct build documentation and clarify architecture compatibility.
  * Restore standard Debian package priority metadata.
  * Add native amd64 and arm64 GitHub build targets.
  * Configure an Ubuntu 26.04 LTS (Resolute) packaging target.
  * Remove stale bytecode, local paths, and unused data from the executable.
  * Validate bundled ELF architecture and Ubuntu glibc compatibility.
  * Declare the system libraries required by the Qt X11 and Wayland backends.

 -- Vadim Bakhrenkov <dev@notolog.app>  Sun, 23 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0000

notolog (1.2.0-1ubuntu1) noble; urgency=medium

  * Initial PPA upload for Ubuntu
  * Added support for admonition notes with themed styling.
  * Added GPU to CPU fallback for ONNX models on insufficient VRAM.
  * Added hardware acceleration support for On Device LLM module.
  * Improved error handling and memory management for AI modules.
  * Improved view mode styling with updated margins and spacing.
  * Removed trailing newlines from code blocks.
  * Fixed font size updates now properly refresh view mode content.
  * Fixed AI model loading blocking the UI thread.
  * Includes all prior project changes up to this version.

 -- Vadim Bakhrenkov <dev@notolog.app>  Sat, 08 Feb 2026 00:00:00 +0000

